{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    /* Explicit `.ts` extensions on a *value* import.
     *
     * `tsup` emits; `tsc` only typechecks (`pnpm typecheck` is `tsc --noEmit`),
     * so nothing here needs to rewrite a specifier and this option costs
     * nothing.
     *
     * It exists because three modules now have to be importable by a plain
     * `.mjs` script — `scripts/check-contrast.mjs`, `build-tokens.mjs`,
     * `build-design-tokens.mjs` — and Node's native type-stripping requires
     * the extension while tsc rejected it without this. The workarounds were
     * accumulating: `contrast.ts` inlines its own copy of the hue list, and
     * `auditContrast` takes its floors as a parameter rather than reading
     * `media.ts`. Both are still fine, but the next one should not have to be
     * invented. */
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    /* A type is imported with `import type`, and nothing else is elided.
     *
     * `dist/` is one file per source module (#301), so an import between two
     * modules is an import between two output files. An import of only types,
     * written as a value import, is dropped today only because esbuild happens
     * to see that nothing uses it at runtime; with this flag the source says so,
     * and what is left is emitted exactly as written. That matters for the
     * server/client split: an edge that survives into `dist/` can put a
     * `'use client'` module in a server module's graph
     * (`scripts/client-boundary.mjs`).
     *
     * It implies `isolatedModules`, which is why that is not set here. */
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    // tsup's dts worker injects its own `baseUrl`, which TS 6 deprecates. Remove
    // once tsup ships a rollup-plugin-dts that no longer sets it (also what
    // currently blocks TS 7 here).
    "ignoreDeprecations": "6.0",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"]
}
